<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gisela of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 985–<a href="/years/1065">1065</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gisela of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> was the first queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">King Stephen</a> I and sister of Emperor Henry II. Her marriage around 996 tied the new Christian Hungarian monarchy to the Ottonian Empire and brought Bavarian clergy and knights to Hungary. After Stephen's death in 1038 she was mistreated under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-orseolo">Peter Orseolo</a> and returned to Bavaria, dying as abbess of Niedernburg in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/passau">Passau</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gisela-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Gisela of Bavaria" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrayal_of_Gisela_of_Hungary_on_the_coronation_pall-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
